# Dotenv files carry secrets once populated. A pattern without a wildcard matches one literal name, so a bare
# `.env` would leave every sibling (.env.local, .env.production, ...) in the context, and the Dockerfile copies the
# whole context into both stages. A pattern is also root-anchored unless it starts with a double-star directory
# prefix, so the sweep is spelled twice; then re-include the public template (order matters: last match wins).
.env*
**/.env*
!.env.example
typechain-types
dist
zkvm/guest/target/
zkvm/host/target/
zkvm/relation-tests/target/
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
*.log
